---
description: Distill durable, verified lessons from this session into the local Markdown library
argument-hint: "[topic or focus]"
---
Review the current conversation and distill reusable knowledge into the private
Markdown library under `~/.pi/memory/`.

Focus: ${ARGUMENTS:-durable project decisions, non-obvious lessons, and reusable technical knowledge}

Load the `persistent-memory` skill and follow its scope, safety, indexing, locking,
and Jujutsu transaction requirements. Inspect relevant indexes and existing notes
before proposing changes. Preserve only a few confirmed, non-sensitive facts likely
to help a future session, choosing the narrowest project or topic scope and merging
with existing notes.

Do not save user preferences or workflow instructions; those belong in
`AGENTS.md` or specialized skills. Do not save feature implementation status;
workspace plans are managed only through the planning skills. Do not save full
transcripts, secrets, speculation, or material already covered by authoritative
instructions or documentation.

If nothing deserves durable storage, leave the library unchanged without creating
a revision. Otherwise summarize the knowledge saved and the note paths changed.
